@startuml

<style>
.OS {
    LineThickness 5.0
}
</style>

skinparam sequenceArrowColor Black
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor White
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor Black
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor Black
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor DarkGray
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor LightYellow
skinparam NoteBorderColor Gray
skinparam NoteTextAlignment left
skinparam ParticipantFontName Courier
skinparam sequenceFontName Courier
skinparam ArrowFontName Courier

title Server <-> Client Sequence Diagram: Underlying-Layer (OS/Transport) Faults (QNX: QNX Dispatch)

actor ExternalClient
participant client_connection
participant qnx_dispatch_engine
participant qnx_dispatch_server
actor ExternalServer

note across : Companion to server_client_sequence_qnx.puml (happy path) and\nserver_client_internal_fault_sequence.puml (library-internal resource limits).\nThis diagram covers faults originating in the OS/transport layer that the\nlibrary detects and reports, but does not itself cause or prevent -\ni.e. non-happy paths of the underlying layers, not user contract misuse\nand not library-internal bookkeeping limits.\nThe Unix Domain counterpart is server_client_os_fault_sequence_linux.puml.

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Connection Refused: Insufficient Permissions (StopReason::kPermission) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalClient -> client_connection : (Start(\n  state_callback,\n  notify_callback\n))
note over client_connection : Invokes state_callback(kStarting)
client_connection -> qnx_dispatch_engine : TryOpenClientConnection(identifier)
note over qnx_dispatch_engine : Returns score::os::Error (EACCES-equivalent)
note over client_connection : Invokes state_callback(kStopping),\nthen state_callback(kStopped)
note left : GetStopReason() == StopReason::kPermission\nPer i_client_connection.h: "highly unlikely to\nhave a successful Restart()" for this reason

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Server Bind/Startup Failure ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalServer -> qnx_dispatch_server : (StartListening(...))
note over qnx_dispatch_server : Returns score::cpp::expected_blank<Error> (error)
note right : IServer::StartListening() reports the startup error;\nthe server does not start accepting connections.

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Peer Crash / Unexpected Disconnect While Ready (StopReason::kClosedByPeer) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

note over client_connection, qnx_dispatch_server : Setup and connection establishment already completed as in\nserver_client_sequence_qnx.puml (omitted here for brevity); both\nendpoints are in their Ready-equivalent state.

note over qnx_dispatch_server : (server process crashes / exits)
client_connection -> qnx_dispatch_engine : ReceiveProtocolMessage(fd, code)
note over qnx_dispatch_engine : => peer closed / broken pipe detected
note over client_connection : Invokes state_callback(kStopping),\nthen state_callback(kStopped)
note left : GetStopReason() == StopReason::kClosedByPeer

note over qnx_dispatch_server : Detected independently on the server side once the OS reports\nthe peer gone; invokes DisconnectCallback(connection) or\nIConnectionHandler::OnDisconnect(connection)

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Communication Error Prevents Continuation (StopReason::kIoError) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalClient -> client_connection : (Send(message) / SendWaitReply(...) / SendWithCallback(...))
client_connection -> qnx_dispatch_engine : SendProtocolMessage(fd, code, message)
note over qnx_dispatch_engine : Returns score::os::Error\n(e.g. corrupted framing, unexpected errno)
note over client_connection : Invokes state_callback(kStopping),\nthen state_callback(kStopped)
note left : GetStopReason() == StopReason::kIoError

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== SendWithCallback: Reply Lost Because Peer Disconnects Mid-Flight ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalClient -> client_connection : (SendWithCallback(message, reply_callback))
client_connection -> qnx_dispatch_engine : SendProtocolMessage(fd, code, message)
note over qnx_dispatch_engine : Delivers the message through the resource manager
note over qnx_dispatch_server : Invokes IConnectionHandler::OnMessageSentWithReply(\n  connection, message\n)
note over qnx_dispatch_server : (server disconnects/crashes\nbefore calling Reply())
note over client_connection : Invokes reply_callback(error)
note left : Per i_client_connection.h: "if the server receives\nthe message but dies or disconnects before the reply\narrives to the client, the error will be passed to\nthe callback; the method itself will not return\nan error."

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== System-Wide Memory Exhaustion (ENOMEM) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalClient -> client_connection : (Start(...) / Send(...))
client_connection -> qnx_dispatch_engine : TryOpenClientConnection(identifier)
note over qnx_dispatch_engine : Or SendProtocolMessage(); returns ENOMEM (system memory\nallocation limit reached)
note left : OS allocation limits are outside the supplied C++\nmemory resource. ENOMEM follows the transport/open\nerror path (kIoError or a Send()/SendWaitReply() error).

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Server-Side Incoming Backpressure Delegated to the OS ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalClient -> client_connection : (Send(message) [rapid, repeated])
client_connection -> qnx_dispatch_engine : SendProtocolMessage(fd, code, message)
note over qnx_dispatch_server : Incoming Send/REQUEST backpressure uses OS channel\nbuffering, not a library ring buffer sized by\nServerConfig::max_queued_sends. Transport calls can\nblock or report OS errors; this is distinct from\nlibrary-side capacity rejection.

@enduml
